<title>GERMANY: Deutsche issues 100 mln, 4-yr step-up bond.</title>
<headline>Deutsche issues 100 mln, 4-yr step-up bond.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-10-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Deutsche Bank AG said on Friday it was issuing a 100 million mark, four-year step-up bond maturing on October 4, 2000, at an issue price of 100.40 for a yield of 4.57 percent.</p>
<p>The bond will pay a coupon of three percent in the first year, four percent in the second year, five percent in the third and seven percent in the fourth year, Deutsche said in a statement.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
